<%# locals: () %>
<%# How much is in the billings list: "n Abrechnungen · HH:MM" (the mockup's
    header line, P2 of the billings plan).

    Its own id, because it must be able to ARRIVE ON ITS OWN: it sits outside
    time_session_groups_list_frame and reads the query that frame answers, so a
    search would narrow the list underneath and leave this figure standing. One
    of TimeSessionGroupsHelper::BILLING_FRAME_DEPENDENT_REGIONS; _groups_list
    streams every one of them back with a frame answer.

    The duration is the policy-scoped sum over ALL filtered billings, not just
    the page: the line reports the answer to the filter, the footer under the
    table reports what is on screen. %>
<% return if @total_filtered_count.nil? %>
<span id="billing_result_summary" class="font-mono tabular-nums text-[15px] font-semibold text-cream-900" data-result-summary>
  <%= t('views.organisations.time_session_groups.index.result_summary',
        count: t('views.organisations.time_session_groups.index.result_billings', count: @total_filtered_count.to_i),
        duration: TimeSession.format_duration(@total_filtered_duration.to_i)) %>
</span>
